## Selected Approach: Approach 1 (Reasoning Continuity Layer)
- **Rationale:** The Reasoning Continuity Layer (RCL) directly targets the primary source of operational friction when building PAEOS—multi-agent context loss across session boundaries. It is well-specified in `backlog/research/PAEOS_REASONING_CONTINUITY_RB_v0.1.md`.
- **Mitigation for Critique:** To address the context window bloat risk, the implementation of the `ContextCompiler` (L03) will feature a strict limit on reasoning history and employ lossy summarization/distillation steps when approaching token thresholds.
